From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: support the Primary TDM link to CS35L41 amps

The Galaxy Z Flip3 drives two CS35L41 amplifiers from Primary TDM: four
32-bit slots at 48 kHz (6.144 MHz bit clock), 16-bit samples, DSP A with
an inverted bit clock on the codec side, as Samsung's lahaina machine
driver sets them up.

sm8250: for PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0, set the 6.144 MHz bit clock at startup and
release it at shutdown, put the AFE port on slots 0-1, and give codec N of
the dai-link TDM slot N, its SCLK as the PLL reference and the slot width.

q6afe: the DT properties qcom,tdm-data-out, qcom,tdm-invert-sync and
qcom,tdm-data-delay were parsed but never reached afe_param_id_tdm_cfg,
so the DSP always framed TDM with no data delay. Pass them through.

q6afe: the response to an LPASS core HW vote carries only the client
handle, which was never stored (and its status was read past the end of
the payload), so every devote sent a stale handle and the DSP failed it
("cmd = 0x100f6 returned error = 0x1"). Keep the handle for the devote,
as downstream does.

cs35l41: implement set_tdm_slot so ASP_WIDTH follows the 32-bit slot
while the word length stays 16 (downstream's cirrus,fixed-width = 32),
and power the amp up after DAPM enables it (POST_PMU), the order
downstream uses. Give the CSPL firmware 15 ms to acknowledge a mailbox
command, as downstream does: Samsung's receiver tuning takes longer than
5 ms to pause.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
